description: Criteria and patterns for adding shared helpers to @achareh/achar
alwaysApply: true
---

# Achar module transfer

When promoting helpers from an Achareh frontend (`app/utils`, etc.) into `@achareh/achar`:

## Transfer only if

- Pure / framework-agnostic (no Nuxt `useCookie`, `import.meta.dev`, Vue `nextTick`, project CSS selectors)
- Not tied to Achareh domain enums, cookie names, route allowlists, toast copy, GA/Intrack, or CDN URL builders
- Reusable across apps (prefer frequently used helpers)

## Do not transfer (explicit)

- `getMimeType`, `getRelativeTitles`
- `regex.ts` validation constants
- `is-fetch-abort.ts` / `isFetchAbortError`
- `web-api.ts` (`webShareApi`, `webOtpApi`)
- `router-tools.ts` (including `isExternalLink`)
- `image-observation.ts`
- `web-socket.ts` / `WebSocketApi`
- cookies, types, query-helper (`resizeFn`), performance, toast, app-handler, app-defaults, custom-ga, event-tracker, layout-routes, afetch-logger, custom-browser-timing
- Thin wrappers that only instantiate APIs already in achar (e.g. `new EventBus()`)

## Adding a module

1. One kebab-case file under `src/modules/<category>/` with a **default export** for a single function
2. Colocated tests: `if (import.meta.vitest) { ... }`
3. Re-export from the category `index.ts` (root already re-exports categories)
4. Document in **both** `docs/en/<category>.md` and `docs/fa/<category>.md` (update the import block)
5. New category → also wire `src/index.ts` and `docs/*/index.md` (+ README tables if present)

Keep public names stable with the source app when migrating (`generateV4UUID`, `round`, …).
